id: pm-csv-ci-v2
title: Pilot Fleet CI v2 quick PR and exhaustive local tiers
description: "Companion: pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve exhaustive default and release validation while reducing PR duplication; measure quick/full coverage and required check latency. Isolated from release caller migration PR #257."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-csv#254","gh:unbraind/pm-csv#258",performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T00:29:21.901Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T08:57:20.430Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[37]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T00:30:34.559Z",codex-sol,"Inspection: #254 both Node jobs failed solely because the 500-case column-ownership corpus exceeded a 2400000ms test timeout. gh --log-failed returned empty; individual jobs API logs confirmed it. Replacing seeded corpus timeouts with explicit seed and transition budgets; no product latency contract is weakened, so no time-scale env is needed. Quick mode uses seeds 1..50 versus 1..500 across seven property loops. accept:packed already proves Bun project/global installs and bunx ephemeral CLI plus tarball extension installs with CSV IO. No standalone markdown/docs checker exists. Release migration PR #257 files remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T00:32:28.090Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck and lint passed. All three edited workflows parsed with the installed yaml parser (actionlint unavailable). Strict health on this development checkout reports an ignored installed pm-github extension/host version skew; this is existing local extension state, not tracked CI state. Will verify health with isolated global configuration. Quick coverage is running; full coverage will follow sequentially to avoid self-contention."
  "2026-11-15T00:34:48.542Z",codex-sol,"Strict health passes with isolated global configuration; the normal developer-global configuration has an unrelated installed extension version skew already tracked by pm-csv-sdyz. Changelog consistency passes. Initial quick coverage found a sampled-roundtrip aggregate expecting too many events for 50 seeds; its required minimum now scales linearly (full still at least 20, quick at least 2), retaining all per-case comparisons. Million-row memory contract remains unchanged and passes. Initial failed-pass timings will not be used as successful benchmarks."
  "2026-11-15T00:39:57.150Z",codex-sol,"Deep job id is deliberately deep, producing deep (22) and deep (26). This keeps a manual branch dispatch from emitting the required test (22)/test (26) contexts and accidentally blocking a PR. Existing CodeQL per-ref PR cancellation was already correct and is retained. Change detection necessarily follows checkout and is the first decision before tool setup/install."
  "2026-11-15T00:44:26.878Z",codex-sol,"Additional cheap validation passed: npm run verify:release-workflow and npm run docstring (25 files, 170 declarations). The corrected 50-seed admission corpus passed with 200 operations, 27 exports and 3 full native-reference round trips. Full-depth minimum remains 20 round trips. Development measurements use Node 24; CI separately validates Node 22 and 26."
  "2026-11-15T00:47:49.309Z",codex-sol,"Synthetic Git-history execution of the workflow change detector passed six scenarios: docs/tracker-only, newline in a docs filename, mixed docs/lockfile, deleted source, newline in a source filename, and manual docs dispatch. Only the first two chose the cheap path. All workflows parse as YAML; actionlint is not installed."
  "2026-11-15T00:48:55.759Z",codex-sol,"The seventh change-detection scenario found and fixed a source-to-docs rename bypass: git name-only with default rename folding emitted only the new docs pathname. Adding --no-renames preserves the deleted source path and correctly selects code=true. The regression fixture demonstrates false before, true after. This is necessary to uphold docs-only gating rather than a design deviation."
  "2026-11-15T01:03:17.102Z",codex-sol,"Slow-hardware hardening also removes the packed-acceptance wrapper test/process deadlines (600/590 seconds). Its fixed host/scenario loops and exact receipt assertions define the work, not elapsed time; the workflow job remains bounded at 120 minutes. #254 passed that test at 471.71 seconds, already close to the old cap. This is preventative removal of the same machine-speed failure class, not an additional failure claimed from #254. The edit precedes this coverage run loading that test file."
  "2026-11-15T01:04:04.293Z",codex-sol,"Timing correction to the preceding comment: process inspection shows packed acceptance launched at nearly the same moment as the wrapper edit, so this quick pass may have loaded the old stricter cap. Both following full coverage and quick release gates will load the updated wrapper, and the touched packed test will also be run explicitly. Assertions and scenario counts are identical in either wrapper; no further runtime-source edits during the measurements."
  "2026-11-15T01:14:12.951Z",codex-sol,"Observed local failure confirms the packed-wrapper deadline problem: the in-flight quick pass loaded the old wrapper and its subprocess was killed at 590.159 seconds. The guard removal had landed after that test process parsed its source. This failed run is excluded from successful timing evidence; rerun quick coverage on frozen final test sources before full coverage and the quick release gate. No source thresholds or assertion scopes changed."
  "2026-11-15T01:17:57.652Z",codex-sol,"Cheap-path audit found existing documentation checks embedded in test/packaging.test.ts and test/shipped-changelog.test.ts, rather than a standalone markdown script. The docs path now runs those plus test/identity-audit.test.ts, preserving public commit/privacy checks for tracker-only PRs. Written design exception: .agents/pm/verify-release-yaml.mjs must select the code path because it is executable release-verification code inside the tracker root; treating it as tracker data would skip the check it can break. The verifier and PR #257 files themselves remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T01:25:42.698Z",codex-sol,"All three final workflows parse successfully as YAML. Final change-detector fixtures pass all eight cases, including source-to-docs rename and executable verifier changes inside the tracker root. The 14 cheap documentation/changelog/identity contract tests passed directly; they are also linked and executed through pm test. The earlier quick pass reported 100 percent lines, branches and functions across all configured sources, with its sole failure being the old packed-wrapper timeout. The frozen-source quick rerun is in progress."
  "2026-11-15T01:31:24.704Z",codex-sol,"Written interpretation/exception for the engines-floor leg: the explicitly requested npm test command itself contains test/packed-custom-fields.test.ts, which invokes accept:packed and therefore packs internally. Keeping npm test and its complete assertions means Node 22 still runs that embedded fixture, although it has no standalone coverage, changelog or pack command. The tier table makes this visible. This preserves the requested test command and existing proof without another skip control; final PR latency measurements will determine whether that remaining duplication is acceptable."
  "2026-11-15T01:46:54.802Z",codex-sol,"Successful quick coverage: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run coverage completed in 1819.14 seconds (30m 19.14s), including build and test compilation, on the shared development host with Node 24.19.0. 473/473 tests passed; zero failures, cancellations and skips. All 13 configured sources were reported at 100 percent lines, branches and functions, with unchanged thresholds and source scope. No late-seed-only branch required a new deterministic fixture. Full coverage has now started sequentially at 500 cases. Timings reflect concurrent host load, not GitHub latency."
  "2026-11-15T02:14:50.482Z",codex-sol,"Full-depth admission corpus passed: seeds 1..500, 2000 operations, 386 exports and 48 native-reference round trips (349.33 seconds). The exhaustive column-ownership corpus remains active; no terminal full-coverage result yet. Proposed-file and tracker-history private-path scan passed. Reserved release workflow, pm-github workflows, verifier scripts and PR #257 file paths have no diff."
  "2026-11-15T02:48:08.084Z",codex-sol,"Written reason for a forthcoming deep-timeout exception: the still-active PM_TEST_DEPTH=full npm run coverage command has exceeded 60 minutes on the required shared-host benchmark. Each deep matrix job runs coverage twice through npm and Bun release gates, so coverage alone exceeds the proposed 120-minute job budget on this host, before packing, audit and installation. Preserve all exhaustive work; select a larger pilot job timeout after the complete measurements. This changes an operational job bound, not test depth or assertions. The sibling recipe will keep 120 minutes as a baseline and require package-specific timing evidence for overrides."
  "2026-11-15T03:07:34.664Z",codex-sol,"Both coverage measurements now pass on frozen test sources. Quick: 1819.14s (30m 19.14s). Full: 4840.58s (80m 40.58s). Each: 473/473 pass, zero fail/cancel/skip, all 13 configured sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions. Full column ownership asserted 500 cases and 2000 transitions. Same shared development host and Node 24.19.0, sequential commands under variable concurrent load; these are raw wall times, not controlled speedup estimates. PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run release:check has started."
  "2026-11-15T03:07:36.965Z",codex-sol,"Final written design exception: ci-deep timeout is 240 minutes rather than 120. Measured full coverage is 80m 40.58s; both npm and Bun release gates run it, so coverage alone needs over 161 minutes per matrix job before packing, audit and setup. A 120-minute guard would cancel exhaustive work on this host. 240 retains an operational limit with headroom. The sibling recipe retains 120 as the fleet baseline and requires measured justification for overrides. Test depths, assertions and coverage thresholds remain exhaustive and unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T03:35:36.158Z",codex-sol,"Additional slow-host proof: packed acceptance completed successfully in the full coverage run at 683.23 seconds (11m 23.23s), beyond its old 590-second subprocess and 600-second test caps. All host/scenario receipt assertions passed. This independently validates removing those harness deadlines in addition to the column corpus timeout fix. The successful standalone quick coverage run completed the same packed proof in 515.40 seconds; host contention varies."
  "2026-11-15T04:04:32.428Z",codex-sol,"PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run release:check passed in 3433.75 seconds (57m 13.75s) on the shared host. This includes typecheck, release workflow verification, build, lint, duplicate detection, docstrings, 473/473 quick-depth tests with 100 percent configured coverage, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, standalone installed npm/Bun/npx/bunx acceptance, changelog consistency, publish attestation and changelog-date verification. Focused touched-test commands are now being executed through pm test --run --progress before publication."
  "2026-11-15T04:24:48.385Z",codex-sol,"Focused tracker execution passed: the seven-file PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --test command passed 47/47 tests in 617.65 seconds; the separate packed-custom-fields command passed 3/3 in 537.64 seconds. Both had zero failure/cancel/skip/todo. These were selected with pm test --run --progress --match; the other linked commands were already executed separately as the measured gates. Latest strict health with required merge drivers passes under isolated global configuration. All requested local proof is complete; publishing the explicit source/docs/tracker file set next."
  "2026-11-15T04:27:21.105Z",codex-sol,"Published PR #258: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/pull/258 at f810b4a861ebd1622c6767660a7e16ba5aada62f. Commit identity audit passes and git log prints only the required public address. Shared-runner hold was inactive at push time. Monitoring required test (22)/test (26) checks; jobs-API created-to-completed timings will be recorded after completion. No review threads or bot comments will be replied to, resolved or reacted to."
  "2026-11-15T04:34:28.871Z",codex-sol,"Required jobs were created at 04:26:22 UTC and remain queued on ubuntu-latest; no test execution yet. At 04:32:39 UTC, a read-only sample of 38 public PM repositories found 15 active GitHub-hosted jobs (14 CI, one Daily Release), zero self-hosted jobs and no unavailable samples. This is a public-PM-only sample, not a total account census. Queue wait will be reported separately from runner execution; it is already material to the 15-minute target. No unrelated jobs, repository variables or branch protection were changed."
  "2026-11-15T04:40:07.636Z",codex-sol,"Review read at f810b4a: Greptile reports no actionable findings (5/5); there are no inline review findings to address. CodeRabbit skipped automatic review and Sourcery reported review-budget exhaustion; these are missing full-review evidence, not approvals. No review replies, reactions or resolutions were posted. Required test (22) started after 8m 20s queueing; test (26) remains queued, making the initial 15-minute target miss dominated by hosted-runner wait. Final jobs-API timings will be retained without excluding queue time."
  "2026-11-15T05:02:10.706Z",codex-sol,"First PR CI run 43676772255 passed both required checks at f810b4a861ebd1622c6767660a7e16ba5aada62f. Jobs API created-to-completed: test (22) 836s (13m 56s), including 500s queue and 336s execution; test (26) 1969s (32m 49s), including 1305s queue and 664s execution. The Node 26 wall target was missed entirely before execution: queue alone exceeded 15 minutes. Runner execution is 5m 36s / 11m 04s. Source changes reduce this package demand; fleet-wide queue relief depends on the companion rollout. No unrelated jobs were canceled or rerouted. The final tracker-receipt head will be checked again, preserving these initial timings."
  "2026-11-15T05:02:12.238Z",codex-sol,"Authorized deep dispatch attempted once with gh workflow run ci-deep.yml --ref ci/quick-pr-tier-deep-local-tier. It refused with HTTP 404 while looking up the new workflow: it is not registered on the default branch yet. No workaround attempted. Full Node 22/26 deep-run evidence remains for the orchestrator after default-branch registration; local full coverage and both hosted quick checks pass."
  "2026-11-15T05:02:13.914Z",codex-sol,"Implementation, local gates and first hosted CI verification are complete. Source commit f810b4a contains all workflow/test/docs changes. Recording the initial queue miss and dispatch receipt, then releasing the claim for orchestrator review. The item remains open; final receipt-only CI and the PR body will carry the final-head wall times. No review findings required a code fix; skipped or quota-limited reviewers remain missing evidence."
  "2026-11-15T05:38:09.477Z",claude-hub,"Orchestrator review: added timeout-minutes 30 to the PR-tier test job and the CodeQL job (quick tier executes in about 6-7 min; on 2026-11-15 three fleet release-gate jobs hung for 90+ min without a timeout until another session cancelled them). test/codeql-dependabot.test.ts and verify:release-workflow pass."
  "2026-11-15T06:12:25.517Z",claude-hub,"Review follow-up (CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63mtjZ, valid): docs/ci-tiers.md documents how deep runs already queued for pm-local recover when PM_LOCAL_DEEP turns off. The fleet controller now cancels the queued CI Deep runs and dispatches one fresh run on main, which resolves to ubuntu-latest, in its fallback step. The manual procedure is documented too."
  "2026-11-15T07:17:40.127Z",codex-sol,"Round 2: rechecked clean worktree and fast-forward state at e3c2b82, preserving the orchestrator timeout and fallback documentation commits. Reclaimed this existing Task. Address PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nGME with generic executable tracker path inclusion and least-privilege CodeQL defaults; address PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nGMK with scaled per-command and acceptance deadlines, process-group cleanup, and a descendant-kill regression plus revert proof. Run only the requested round-2 gates; do not repeat completed full-depth benchmarks or interact with review threads."
  "2026-11-15T07:18:15.931Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nGME: both CodeQL triggers now use the requested ordered paths, re-including mjs/cjs/js/ts anywhere in the tracker. Workflow defaults deny all token permissions; the existing job permissions remain explicit. PR change detection recognizes the same four executable extensions, including nested tracker directories. Template documentation updated. CodeQL workflow contract tests pass 2/2; final gates will run after the process deadline fix."
  "2026-11-15T07:22:27.726Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nGMK implementation: asynchronous sequential acceptance commands preserve all scenario assertions while each command has a 5-minute safety budget and the packed test has a 30-minute aggregate budget, both scaled by PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE (default 1; deep 3). Unix expiry SIGKILLs the detached process group; Windows taskkill terminates the tree. Outer acceptance timeout forwards termination through the nested supervisor before a final hard group kill. Tests pass 4/4 at scale 1 and 4/4 at scale 3. Revert proof: temporarily changed group SIGKILL to direct-child-only SIGKILL; the new direct deadline regression failed with sleeping grandchild must be dead (exit 1), fixture cleanup killed the survivor, and restoring group termination passed all 4 tests. Invalid scale factors fail closed. Final quick coverage and touched acceptance gates next."
  "2026-11-15T07:27:55.844Z",codex-sol,"Round-2 touched gate passed through pm test: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --test test/acceptance-process.test.ts test/codeql-dependabot.test.ts test/packed-custom-fields.test.ts test/packaging.test.ts test/shipped-changelog.test.ts test/identity-audit.test.ts completed 23/23, zero failures/cancellations/skips, in 280572 ms. PM linked-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment preserves the receipt. Direct gates passed: npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run verify:release-workflow, npm run changelog:check, npm run docstring and npm run duplicates. No actionlint installed; all three workflows parsed with YAML unique-key validation. The actual PR Bash classifier passed 12 root/nested executable and docs/tracker cases. Starting the single requested round-2 quick coverage run with thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T07:51:08.427Z",codex-sol,"Round-2 final gate receipt for PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nGMK: the single requested PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run coverage passed 478/478, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, and 100% lines/branches/functions across the unchanged 13 configured source files. Linked-command elapsed time was 1349337 ms (22m 29.34s); outer pm invocation including orchestration was 1351.00 seconds. Coverage thresholds, source scope and ignore configuration are unchanged. Fresh final runner tests pass 4/4 at default scale and 4/4 at scale 3; nested cleanup uses the same one-second grace as the real wrapper. Final test compilation and lint also pass after that test-budget calibration. Combined touched/docs/identity/CodeQL gate passed 23/23, including CodeQL 2/2. All other requested gates passed as recorded above. Revert proof remains exit 1 with the surviving-grandchild assertion when group killing is temporarily replaced by direct-child-only killing; restored implementation passes. macOS and Windows termination paths are implemented but not executed on this Linux host. No review threads were replied to or resolved, no item was closed, and release migration files remain untouched. The existing queue-inclusive latency gap and deep workflow registration receipt remain with the companion rollout; no repeat deep dispatch or full benchmark was needed for this round."
  "2026-11-15T08:26:47.181Z",codex-sol,"Round 3: fast-forward check is current at 85d0bdb and the worktree was clean. Reclaimed this existing Task. Address the two nested-cancellation reports (PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nlQN and PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63ng42) with the existing bounded escalation sequence and a signal-driven descendant regression. Add pure Windows npm/npx command selection for PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nlQJ, and taskkill outcome classification for PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nlQL. Preserve deadline semantics and unrelated workflow/release files. Run only the requested round-3 gates, including one quick coverage run; do not repeat prior full benchmarks or deep dispatch. Review threads remain for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-15T08:32:43.674Z",codex-sol,"Round-3 implementation and red/green proof: external SIGTERM and SIGINT now reuse the configured deadline grace/escalation before exiting 143/130, giving nested supervisors time to forward termination. Leaf operations retain their zero-grace group kill and the deadline path retains its existing timeout semantics. The new outer/supervisor/child/grandchild fixture verifies both external signals. Restoring immediate SIGTERM exit makes the regression fail with cancelled nested child must be dead (exit 1); cleanup kills all fixture PIDs. Reverting Windows selection to direct spawning fails the npm/npx JavaScript-entry assertion (exit 1). Reverting taskkill status checking fails its cleanup-error assertion (exit 1). All three fixes restored. Windows selection uses npm_execpath, then the Node-adjacent npm bin entries; only absent entries permit a quoted shell fallback with expansion/control characters rejected. Taskkill status and stderr are surfaced for real cleanup failures; status 128 with a not-found/no-running-instance diagnostic retains the original timeout because the root already exited. Runner tests pass 9/9 at scale 1 and 9/9 at scale 3, zero failure/cancel/skip. Typecheck, test compilation, final lint, docstrings, duplicates and changelog check pass. Starting the one required round-3 quick coverage gate; source scope and thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T08:57:19.518Z",codex-sol,"Round-3 final receipt: the single required PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run coverage passed 483/483 with zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo. All 13 unchanged configured sources meet 100% lines, branches and functions; independent LCOV counter comparison confirms all hits. Linked-command time was 1382047 ms (23m 02.05s); outer PM orchestration wall time was 1384.11 seconds. Final runner gates passed 9/9 at scale 1 (10406.93 ms) and 9/9 at scale 3 (22712.63 ms), including both existing deadline cases, Windows selection/classification and external SIGTERM/SIGINT nested cleanup. Typecheck, test compilation, final lint, docstrings, duplicates and changelog check passed. All three revert proofs failed their targeted regression with exit 1, then restored source passed the gates. No source/threshold/ignore changes were made during coverage. Runtime changes are confined to scripts/acceptance-process.ts; only its tests, tiny fixture and this tracker accompany the fix. Native Windows/macOS runtime behavior was not executed on this Linux host; Windows decisions are covered by pure unit tests. Review threads PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nlQN, PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63ng42, PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nlQJ and PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s63nlQL remain for the orchestrator. No release/workflow files or repository settings changed; no repeat full benchmark/deep dispatch was needed. Releasing the claim and leaving the Task in progress."
